                          अपूर्णध्रुवम् २५ । इति`, GONE, and its condition
                          returning as `यदि घोषणासूचकः समम् ० आदि` — the same
                          test, now opening the resolving branch instead of
                          refusing on it. The refusal did not disappear; it
                          moved inward to `यदि वस्तुप्रविष्टिः समम् ० आदि
                          प्रत्यागमनम् अपूर्णध्रुवम् ३६ । इति`, which fires
                          only when the walk actually finds nothing. The other
                          four new ones are the walk's own tests: the struct-
                          name match, the field-name compare, the first-write
                          guard, and `क्षेत्रमिलितम्`.
     +2 यावत्             the two walks — over `अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञा*` for the
                          struct, then over its parameter entries for the field.
     +1 अन्यथा            the branch the former refusal became.
     ±0 प्रत्यागमनम्      16 rewritten, 16 in place. A cause renumbering cannot
                          move this key, and its stillness across a change that
                          touched sixteen `प्रत्यागमनम्` lines is the cleanest
                          evidence the decomposition renamed rather than added.

   AND IT RECONCILES WITH `w250-shares.rs`, WHICH IS WORTH MORE THAN EITHER PIN.
   That census splits on the statement's FIRST token and reads
   (2798, 2722, 5520). The totals agree at 5520; 2798 + 592 = 3390 and
   2722 − 592 = 2130. The bridge is `public-bindings`, a number neither
   instrument is free to choose. Note that this row CANNOT distinguish the two
   classifications on its own evidence — it added no public binding, so the
   +5/+5 is identical under both models. The paragraph above at the 2026-09-09
   entry says why that matters: a row without a public binding confirms both
